Article 14: Where, due to the seller's reasons, the buyer fails to obtain the certificate of title to the immovable property upon expiry of the following time limits, unless the parties have special agreements, the seller shall bear liability for breach of contract:
(1) the time limit for handling immovable property registration as stipulated in the commercial housing sales contract;
(2) where the subject matter of the commercial housing sales contract is a house not yet completed, 90 days from the date of delivery and use of the house;
(3) where the subject matter of the commercial housing sales contract is a completed house, 90 days from the date of conclusion of the contract.
Where the contract has no stipulation on liquidated damages or the amount of losses is difficult to determine, the amount may be calculated based on the total paid purchase price, by reference to the standard prescribed by the People's Bank of China for financial institutions to calculate interest on overdue loans.
